65.55419921875,984.5999755859375],"color":"#3f789e","font_size":24,"flags":{},"description":"Same boxes, scores and thresholds (score 0.5, IoU 0.5). F_VN_NonMaxSuppression ignores class, so the stacked washer is suppressed by the better-scoring nut on top of it. F_VN_NonMaxSuppressionExp takes ipClassIndcies and only suppresses boxes of the same class, so the washer survives. fEta 1 keeps the overlap threshold constant; nTopK 0 considers every box."},{"id":4,"title":"4a. Plain NMS result","bounding":[4480,1540,3530,510],"color":"#3f789e","font_size":24,"flags":{},"description":"Three boxes: the washer under the nut is missing."},{"id":5,"title":"4b. Class-aware NMS result","bounding":[4480,2120,3930,790],"color":"#3f789e","font_size":24,"flags":{},"description":"Four boxes: one per part, including the washer under the nut."}],"config":{},"extra":{"filemeta":{"name":"Class-Aware Duplicate Removal with NonMaxSuppressionExp","description":" This example compares plain and class-aware non-maximum suppression on a detector output where two different part types overlap, using F_VN_NonMaxSuppressionExp .","tags":["Assembly Verification","Multi-Class Detection","Object Detection","Robotics"]},"__aiIds":{"e8042134-77a9-4cc6-85b4-6eb6630946fc":"img","3079782a-37b8-4345-ad2f-d325d5a8d78d":"tcR","6d8a42ef-6a6a-4ec4-b88d-c21013a8c89b":"cR","c47182f8-8502-4110-8746-6a19bb09be4a":"tcS","655a9c32-cf0e-4be3-aed5-faf4a2f16d05":"cS","8ac0cdaf-f826-44b3-a698-060e953b7d42":"tcC","f7864ca8-b683-4703-a5f6-89c5bdd10346":"cC","634a17f0-28c9-4449-9baa-e0fb92033d40":"rgbAll","1fa2f602-17c0-4825-a2a2-7514905ad376":"rgbP","754e06d7-73ee-4d58-a258-5840d75567ef":"rgbX","8aac669f-f3b7-47a4-b89c-f49f39c97530":"yel","33947f50-5b11-409f-9ebb-0e5543fa5215":"cyn","e390e247-818a-4991-9341-32fdddcc8607":"grn","18568049-febb-46bb-a2c0-6c1a9cdcfb4a":"b0","e83cffd1-d609-4b7b-85c9-cb1d83452fef":"ar0","c9c06570-a789-443e-b03b-545628bcd344":"as0","336c606a-35bf-4f97-b1b5-a76ff5445f63":"ac0","c7cdf42a-baff-4c44